filter-graph: always pass the soft volume when the graph applies the volume

impl_set_props() added softVolumes/softMute only when the channelVolumes or
mute differed from the graph's own copy. A Props that repeats the current
volume, or carries mute alone, reached audioconvert with channelVolumes and
no softVolumes, so audioconvert applied the channelVolumes in software as
well as the graph's control, until the next real volume change.

Against PipeWire 1.6.10 (applies unchanged to 1.6.11, with or without
filter-graph-latency.patch).

diff --git a/spa/plugins/filter-graph/filter-graph.c b/spa/plugins/filter-graph/filter-graph.c
